00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:28.760
And eventually, they were both adopted together, these little brothers, by this young woman named Carrie.
最终，这对小兄弟被一位叫凯莉的年轻女士一起领养了。

298
00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:31.620
And I'm still in touch with her.
我和她至今仍有联系。

299
00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.700
She still sends me pictures of these guys.
她还会给我发这些小家伙的照片。

300
00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.040
It's the sweetest thing.
真是太贴心了。

301
00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.720
So I reached out to find out how they're doing.
所以我联系了他们，想看看他们过得怎么样。

302
00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.220
She said they are now 12 years old.
她说他们现在已经12岁了。

303
00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:40.940
Wow.
哇。

304
00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:48.740
She said that Dunder, who used to be kind of the more rascally outgoing one, has become a little crankier in his old age.
她说Dunder，以前那个比较淘气外向的家伙，上了年纪后变得有点暴躁了。

305
00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:51.220
He kind of hides when people come over now.
现在有人来家里时，他还会躲起来。

306
00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:57.660
Whereas Mifflin, who was always kind of the shy one, loves to get pets from anybody who visits.
而Mifflin，以前总是比较害羞的那一个，现在却很喜欢让来访的任何人抚摸他。

307
00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:03.880
So, you know, Carrie also ended up being a foster parent for Kittens at Kitten Rescue.
你知道，Carrie后来还成了Kitten Rescue（小猫救援组织）的寄养家长。

308
00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:15.980
And she told me that Dunder and Mifflin have helped to foster uncle, or as she calls it, funcled, over 80 kittens in the past 12 years.
她告诉我，在过去的12年里，Dunder和Mifflin帮忙当了80多只小猫的“寄养叔叔”，或者她称之为“趣叔”。

309
00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:19.620
And that they're very, very good with all the little kittens that she fosters.
而且他们对她寄养的所有小猫都非常非常好。

310
00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:31.540
It's funny, because when I was working with Kitten Rescue, I think I gave an interview where I said that I had fostered and found homes for over 13 cats.
说来有趣，因为我以前在Kitten Rescue工作时，记得有一次采访中我说过，我寄养并为13只以上的猫找到了家。

311
00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.300
And that got printed as I had 13 cats.
结果被印成了我有13只猫。

312
00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.340
And it took me years to get that corrected.
我花了好几年才把这个错误纠正过来。

313
00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:42.840
It was on, like, Wikipedia forever.
它在维基百科上挂了很久。

314
00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:47.520
And every time I would do an interview, someone would say, tell me about your 13 cats.
每次我接受采访，总有人会说，跟我聊聊你的那13只猫吧。

315
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.760
And I would be like, can we please?
我就会说，咱们能别这样吗？

316
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.260
I fostered 13 cats.
我只是寄养过13只猫。

317
00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.980
And not at the same time, like, one by one.
而且不是同时养的，是分批寄养的。

318
00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.180
Right, over years.
没错，是好几年间的事。

319
00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.360
Well, incidentally, Kitten Rescue is where I adopted Sunny.
顺便提一下，我就是在Kitten Rescue领养的Sunny。

320
00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.620
And I'm going to link to them in our show notes.
我会在节目介绍里放上他们的链接。

321
00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:02.840
They are such a great organization.
他们是一个非常棒的组织。

322
00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:08.540
And I also have some really fun photos of Dunder and Mifflin from when they were kittens as well as now.
我还有一些Dunder和Mifflin小时候以及现在的超可爱照片。

323
00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.360
And we'll put it in our Instagram stories.
我们会把它们发到我们的Instagram快拍里。

324
00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:11.320
Oh, I can't wait.
噢，我等不及了。

325
00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:16.280
You guys, as Jenna was sharing the story, I just was remembering all these memories.
伙计们，当Jenna分享这个故事时，我脑海里涌现出了好多回忆。

326
00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:25.040
When we would walk onto set, there were these side doors that we would come onto the set of the Dunder Mifflin bullpen from our trailers.
以前我们走进片场时，会从拖车那边经过侧门进入Dunder Mifflin的办公区。

327
00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.400
We had a wall of, like, announcements.
我们有一面墙，上面贴满了各种公告。

328
00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:32.480
Like, if someone had a baby, we'd put the photo up there or, you know, just any little thing.
比如谁生了宝宝，我们就会把照片贴在那儿，或者诸如此类的小事。

329
00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:36.220
I remember, like, when you were in a poker tournament, like, we put a little thing up there.
我记得你参加扑克锦标赛的时候，我们也贴了张小纸条在那儿。

330
00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.960
Just anything that was going on in our lives, cast and crew.
就是演员和剧组成员生活中发生的任何事。

331
00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:44.600
And then you would walk by and you would read and you'd be like, oh, my gosh, Patrick, you know, you're getting married.
你走过去读到的时候会说，天哪，Patrick，你要结婚了。

332
00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:45.320
That's so great.
那太棒了。

333
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:46.280
There'd be little announcements.
上面总会有各种小公告。

334
00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.520
Well, there was a photo of Dunder and Mifflin.
当时就有一张Dunder和Mifflin的照片。

335
00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.400
We had printed off on Searock.
我们用Searock打印出来的。

336
00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:51.820
A little flyer.
一张小传单。

337
00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.760
Yeah, a little flyer that hung there.
对，一张挂在那儿的小传单。

338
00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:55.880
And we would walk past it every day.
我们每天都会从它旁边走过。

339
00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:58.920
And we left it up even after they were adopted, just like their photo.
即使在他们被领养后，我们也一直留着它，就像留着他们的照片一样。

340
00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:00.840
Oh, I love that.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

341
00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.720
I want to see what they look like now.
我想看看他们现在长什么样。

342
00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:03.280
I know.
我知道。

343
00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.100
They're so cute.
他们太可爱了。

344
00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.500
Well, that's all I've got.
好了，我要说的就这些。

345
00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.380
Should we take a break and then come back and...
我们要不要休息一下，回来后再……

346
00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.300
Yeah, let's get into this episode.
好，让我们开始聊聊这一集吧。

347
00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.660
There's so much fun stuff to discuss.
有很多有趣的内容可以讨论。

348
00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:31.860
This episode kicks off with a very exuberant Merry Christmas from Dwight and Jim, who, if you remember, are now the heads of the party planning committee.
这一集开头，Dwight和Jim非常热情地祝大家圣诞快乐，如果你还记得的话，他们现在是派对策划委员会的负责人。

349
00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.760
Yeah, they're still in charge of the parties.
没错，他们还在负责派对的事。

350
00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:37.000
I have to say, they do a good job this year.
我得说，他们今年干得不错。

351
00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:37.780
They do.
确实如此。

352
00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.000
This is a great Christmas party.
这真是一场很棒的圣诞派对。

353
00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.300
The decor is great.
装饰得很棒。

354
00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:41.820
They have some great ideas.
他们有一些很棒的点子。

355
00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:46.180
Well, I have a reason for that I'm going to share with you that was in Deleted Scenes.
嗯，我有一个原因要和你们分享，那是被删减片段里的内容。

356
00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:47.160
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

357
00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:52.200
Well, next up, Dwight has a talking head where he shares that he put his diabolical plan on hold.
那么，接下来，德怀特有一个访谈镜头，他分享说他搁置了他的邪恶计划。

358
00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:53.860
I have to share something.
我得分享点什么。

359
00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:59.140
So, when I was talking to Joya about this episode, she said,
所以，当我和乔亚聊到这一集时，她说，

360
00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:08.140
Oh, Angela, I meant to reach out to you about Scott's Tots because we launched a diabolical blog to coincide with Dwight's diabolical plan.
哦，安吉拉，我本来想联系你聊聊《斯科特的托儿们》那一集，因为我们为了配合德怀特的邪恶计划，专门开了一个邪恶博客。

361
00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:13.600
Yes, it was a weekly blog about Dwight's diabolical plan.
没错，那是一个关于德怀特邪恶计划的每周博客。

362
00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.080
You can still see the blog entries.
你现在还能看到那些博客文章。

363
00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.960
I'm going to put a link to them in our stories.
我会把链接放到我们的快拍里。

364
00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.380
I'm showing Jenna a picture of what the front page looks like.
我正在给珍娜看首页长什么样。

365
00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.620
Oh, it's the coup de Dwight.
哦，是“德怀特政变”。

366
00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.780
The diabolical blog by Dwight K.
德怀特·K·施鲁特撰写的邪恶博客。

367
00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:26.240
Schrute.
施鲁特。

368
00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:29.800
So, I'll put that in our stories, but I thought that was so fun.
所以，我会把它放到我们的快拍里，我觉得这太有趣了。

369
00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:36.320
After this Dwight talking head, Jenna, there was a Jim talking head that got deleted.
在这个德怀特访谈镜头之后，珍娜，还有一个被删掉的吉姆访谈镜头。

370
00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:41.500
It's in the extended producer's cut, but I want to read to you a little bit of it from the shooting draft.
它在制作人加长版里，但我想从拍摄剧本里读一点给你们听。

371
00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:42.000
Okay.
好的。

372
00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:43.800
It was actually really sweet.
其实真的很温馨。

373
00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:46.260
Jim says,
吉姆说，

374
00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.060
Lately, there have been serious rumors that our company might go bankrupt.
最近，有严重的传言说我们公司可能会破产。

375
00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.560
David Wallace asked me to keep morale high.
大卫·华莱士让我保持士气高昂。

376
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.120
Then there's B-roll.
然后是空镜画面。

377
00:18:54.640 --> 00:19:02.360
And the B-roll captures people taking turns going into Jim's office while Jim actually listens and jots down notes.
空镜画面里拍到大家轮流走进吉姆的办公室，而吉姆真的在听并做着记录。

378
00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.220
Angela goes in, Kevin, Kelly, Stanley.
安吉拉进去了，还有凯文、凯莉、斯坦利。

379
00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.440
Jim's talking head continues.
吉姆的访谈镜头继续。

380
00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:10.760
I asked around what people wanted with Christmas.
我问了大家对圣诞节有什么想法。

381
00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:12.740
Get creative, I said.
我说，发挥创意吧。

382
00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.960
And people weren't really creative exactly.
但大家其实并没有什么创意。

383
00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:20.240
They said Secret Santa, karaoke, food, pretty much what we usually have, which is great.
他们说交换礼物、卡拉OK、食物，基本上就是我们平时有的那些，这也很棒。

384
00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.440
Then there's B-roll of Jim and Dwight dusting off old decorations.
接着是吉姆和德怀特清理旧装饰的空镜画面。

385
00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.380
Jim continues to talk.
吉姆继续说着。

386
00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.700
People usually argue about food, so I told everyone to bring their favorites.
大家通常会为了食物争论，所以我告诉每个人带他们最喜欢的食物来。

387
00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.320
Then there's B-roll.
然后是空镜画面。

388
00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.540
Angela laying out carrots and celery.
安吉拉摆放着胡萝卜和芹菜。

389
00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.260
Kevin with an enormous chocolate cake.
凯文端着一个巨大的巧克力蛋糕。

390
00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:39.120
Pam brings in a lasagna.
帕姆带了一份千层面。

391
00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:43.880
And finally, Creed emptying a large can of beans into a glass serving bowl.
最后，克里德把一大罐豆子倒进了一个玻璃碗里。

392
00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:45.200
Jim continues.
吉姆继续说。

393
00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:49.760
I made a very organized sign-up sheet for karaoke so there's no fighting.
我做了一张非常有条理的卡拉OK报名表，这样就不会有争执了。

394
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:54.780
B-roll of Jim holding up a clipboard next to the karaoke machine with a
空镜画面是吉姆拿着一块写字板站在卡拉OK机旁，上面用红字写着

395
00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.480
must-take-turns written on it in red letters.
必须轮流演唱。

396
00:19:58.060 --> 00:20:00.700
Kelly, Andy, and Kevin crowd around to sign up.
凯莉、安迪和凯文围过来报名。

397
00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.640
Jim continues talking.
吉姆继续说着。

398
00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.400
And no crying.
而且不许哭。

399
00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:07.900
Jim hangs up a banner in the conference room.
吉姆在会议室挂起了一条横幅。

400
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.140
It says, Merry Christmas.
上面写着，圣诞快乐。

401
00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.680
Santa hates tears.
圣诞老人讨厌眼泪。

402
00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.740
And then lastly, Jim says,
最后，吉姆说，

403
00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.860
I made Phyllis Santa, fulfilling a lifelong dream.
我让菲利斯扮成圣诞老人，圆了她一生的梦想。

404
00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.240
Phyllis hugs Jim and will not let go.
菲利斯拥抱吉姆，不肯松手。

405
00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.060
Jim tries to subtly break free.
吉姆试图不动声色地挣脱。

406
00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:25.120
And then Jim ends this talking head with this.
然后吉姆用这段话结束了采访。

407
00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.460
I'm doing a good job, I think.
我想我做得不错。

408
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.340
Because this year, I care.
因为今年，我上心了。

409
00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.300
I know.
我知道。

410
00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:30.940
It's weird.
这很奇怪。

411
00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.980
He shrugs, happy.
他耸耸肩，很高兴。

412
00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.440
That is so sweet.
真是太贴心了。

413
00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:36.320
I know.
我知道。

414
00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.800
It was a great talking head.
那是一段很棒的采访。

415
00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.860
And it really showed how Jim was invested in making this a good party.
它确实展示了吉姆是多么投入地想把这次聚会办好。

416
00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.600
This is good management.
这就是好的管理。

417
00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.420
This just reminds me of how Greg Daniels would treat us.
这让我想起格雷格·丹尼尔斯是如何对待我们的。

418
00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.200
He would come around and he would say,
他会走过来问我们，

419
00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:51.080
What do you think should happen to your character this year?
你觉得今年你的角色应该发生什么？

420
00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:51.880
Yes.
没错。

421
00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.040
And you'd be like, I have ideas.
你会说，我有想法。

422
00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.760
Thank you for asking.
谢谢你的询问。

423
00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:59.660
So now Erin is going to make an announcement to the bullpen.
现在艾琳要向办公区宣布一件事。

424
00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:05.520
She is pleading with whoever is her secret Santa to please stop sending gifts.
她恳求她的神秘圣诞老人不要再送礼物了。

425
00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:11.620
Her secret Santa is doing a 12 Days of Christmas themed gift for her.
她的神秘圣诞老人正在送她一套“圣诞十二日”主题的礼物。

426
00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:15.980
And she says that her cat killed the turtle dove.
她说她的猫弄死了斑鸠。

427
00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:19.040
The French hens are making a nest in her hair.
法国母鸡在她的头发里筑巢。

428
00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:22.620
She has scratches down her face.
她的脸上全是抓痕。

429
00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.840
She's having a hard time with this gift.
她被这份礼物折磨得够呛。

430
00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

431
00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.860
She seems really miserable.
她看起来真的很痛苦。

432
00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:35.460
Well, I wanted to share with you guys that the DVD commentary for this episode is Ellie Kemper, Mindy Kaling, and Claire Scanlon.
我想告诉大家，这一集的DVD评论音轨是由艾丽·坎伯、敏迪·卡灵和克莱尔·斯坎伦录制的。

433
00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:36.640
Oh, great.
太棒了。

434
00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:37.000
Yeah.
是啊。

435
00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:40.240
And they talked a little bit about this scratch on Ellie's face.
她们聊到了艾丽脸上的那道抓痕。

436
00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:46.880
Mindy shared that they had a test model that they did a few different types of scratches on and took pictures of.
敏迪分享说，她们做了一个测试模型，在上面画了几种不同类型的抓痕并拍了照。

437
00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:50.360
And then Mindy had to pick which scratch she liked.
然后敏迪必须选出她喜欢的那一种。

438
00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:50.920
Yes.
没错。

439
00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:55.440
Randy said our makeup artist, Laverne, created the effects of the scratch.
兰迪说我们的化妆师拉文制作了抓痕的效果。

440
