746
00:35:57.500 --> 00:35:59.680
He's like, it's cold down there.
他说，下面很冷。

747
00:35:59.980 --> 00:36:01.920
It's like he lists all these things.
他列举了所有这些理由。

748
00:36:01.920 --> 00:36:03.240
And she's like, okay, fine.
她说，好吧，行吧。

749
00:36:03.240 --> 00:36:05.740
And lets him go hand out the checks.
然后让他去发支票了。

750
00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:07.200
But he's looking for Matt.
但他其实是想找马特。

751
00:36:07.200 --> 00:36:08.680
But Matt's not there.
但马特不在那儿。

752
00:36:08.820 --> 00:36:09.820
He's out on a delivery.
他出去送货了。

753
00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:12.400
And Daryl's like, I'll take it.
然后达里尔说，我来拿吧。

754
00:36:12.460 --> 00:36:13.180
I'll give it to him.
我交给他。

755
00:36:14.060 --> 00:36:17.040
And Oscar's like, no, no, I can wait.
奥斯卡却说，不，不，我可以等。

756
00:36:18.480 --> 00:36:19.400
Daryl's on to him.
达里尔看穿了他。

757
00:36:19.400 --> 00:36:19.960
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

758
00:36:20.460 --> 00:36:21.860
Have you ever done something like this?
你做过类似的事吗？

759
00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:22.620
Of course.
当然。

760
00:36:22.620 --> 00:36:23.720
We all have.
我们都做过。

761
00:36:24.080 --> 00:36:29.460
I remember when I was like younger, like a kid, I had a little bit of a crush on one
我记得我小时候，还是个孩子的时候，我有点喜欢上了一个

762
00:36:29.460 --> 00:36:30.440
of the boys in my neighborhood.
住在我们街区的男孩。

763
00:36:30.860 --> 00:36:33.160
And I used to look out the window.
我经常往窗外看。

764
00:36:33.520 --> 00:36:39.460
And when I would see him outside, like playing soccer or something, I would conveniently need
每当看到他在外面踢足球什么的，我就会找个借口

765
00:36:39.460 --> 00:36:40.540
to go to the mailbox.
去邮箱那边。

766
00:36:40.820 --> 00:36:41.000
Yeah.
是啊。

767
00:36:41.300 --> 00:36:45.660
Hoping, hoping that he would like wave at me or something, that we could have a run in.
希望能碰巧让他跟我打个招呼什么的，能有个偶遇。

768
00:36:46.240 --> 00:36:47.480
It never happened.
但这从未发生过。

769
00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:54.740
And I mean, in college, I watched Bassmasters because the guy I liked was really into watching
还有，大学的时候，我看了《鲈鱼大师》，因为我喜欢的那个男生特别爱看

770
00:36:55.260 --> 00:36:59.780
Bassmasters, watching people fish and talk about the hooks they used and the lures and
《鲈鱼大师》，看人们钓鱼，谈论他们用的鱼钩、鱼饵以及

771
00:36:59.780 --> 00:37:00.240
the whatnot.
诸如此类的东西。

772
00:37:01.540 --> 00:37:02.920
These are the things you do.
这就是你会做的事。

773
00:37:03.100 --> 00:37:03.420
Yeah.
是啊。

774
00:37:03.500 --> 00:37:04.380
When you have a crush.
当你暗恋某人的时候。

775
00:37:04.600 --> 00:37:04.800
Yeah.
是啊。

776
00:37:04.940 --> 00:37:08.480
When all of a sudden this guy is like, I think on Sunday I'm going to watch Bassmasters.
当那个男生突然说，我觉得周日我要看《鲈鱼大师》时。

777
00:37:08.580 --> 00:37:09.620
I'm like, oh, yeah, it's so great.
我就说，哦，是啊，那节目太棒了。

778
00:37:09.860 --> 00:37:11.720
That guy, the host, he's hilarious.
那个主持人，他太搞笑了。

779
00:37:12.100 --> 00:37:13.700
And then you're like, who is the host?
然后你就会想，主持人是谁？

780
00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:15.860
There is no host of Bassmasters.
《鲈鱼大师》根本没有主持人。

781
00:37:15.880 --> 00:37:17.120
What is Bassmasters?
什么是《鲈鱼大师》？

782
00:37:18.060 --> 00:37:20.960
And you couldn't Google back then because it was just invented.
而且那时候你还没法用谷歌搜索，因为谷歌才刚发明。

783
00:37:21.140 --> 00:37:21.640
I know.
我知道。

784
00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:22.360
Yeah.
是啊。

785
00:37:22.420 --> 00:37:23.680
It wasn't invented yet.
那时候还没发明出来呢。

786
00:37:23.680 --> 00:37:24.880
There was no internet.
根本没有互联网。

787
00:37:25.340 --> 00:37:26.880
I will never let that one go.
我永远不会让这件事过去的。

788
00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:27.240
I know.
我知道。

789
00:37:27.340 --> 00:37:27.840
It's too fun.
太好玩了。

790
00:37:27.840 --> 00:37:28.180
Clearly.
显然是这样。

791
00:37:28.360 --> 00:37:28.900
It's too fun.
太好玩了。

792
00:37:28.900 --> 00:37:30.420
It's one of my favorite bits now.
这现在成了我最喜欢的梗之一。

793
00:37:32.240 --> 00:37:37.580
Well, Michael is still sitting in the chair upstairs trying to get people to sit on his
好吧，迈克尔现在还坐在楼上的椅子里，试图让别人坐在他的

794
00:37:37.580 --> 00:37:37.860
lap.
大腿上。

795
00:37:38.040 --> 00:37:43.740
He is now, like, wrestling Ryan onto his lap while saying, I need this.
他现在正强行把瑞安按在他腿上，一边说，我需要这个。

796
00:37:43.860 --> 00:37:44.540
I need this.
我需要这个。

797
00:37:44.740 --> 00:37:51.020
Claire and Mindy also talked in the commentary that when Jim steps in and is like, hey, you
克莱尔和明迪在评论中也提到，当吉姆介入并说，嘿，你

798
00:37:51.020 --> 00:37:56.320
know, Michael, you can't, you know, you can't grab someone in the office and say, I need
知道吗，迈克尔，你不能，你知道，你不能在办公室里抓住某人说，我需要

799
00:37:56.320 --> 00:37:56.720
this.
这个。

800
00:37:56.820 --> 00:37:58.620
While forcing them onto your lap.
同时还强迫他们坐在你的大腿上。

801
00:37:58.620 --> 00:38:00.500
It makes me laugh out loud every time.
每次看到这儿我都会笑出声。

802
00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:01.840
John's delivery is so good.
约翰的演绎太棒了。

803
00:38:02.120 --> 00:38:05.320
They shared on the commentary that he kept laughing in so many takes.
他们在评论音轨里分享过，他拍了好多次都在不停地笑场。

804
00:38:05.840 --> 00:38:06.600
That's the thing.
关键就在这儿。

805
00:38:06.740 --> 00:38:10.880
Like, when you know something is funny, even though you have to deliver it, it, like, it
就像，当你明知某件事很好笑，即便你必须把它演出来，它，就像，它

806
00:38:10.880 --> 00:38:12.400
tickles you while you're doing it.
会让你在表演时忍不住发笑。

807
00:38:13.800 --> 00:38:19.880
This scene is going to end with Michael putting his Santa hat into the punch bowl and storming
这一幕的结尾是迈克尔把他的圣诞帽扔进潘趣酒碗里，然后气冲冲地

808
00:38:19.880 --> 00:38:20.220
out.
走出去。

809
00:38:20.400 --> 00:38:20.960
So rude.
太粗鲁了。

810
00:38:21.380 --> 00:38:24.200
Mindy talked about something in the commentary I thought was really interesting.
敏迪在评论音轨里提到了一个我觉得非常有意思的点。

811
00:38:24.460 --> 00:38:29.540
She said at 8 minutes 39 seconds, when Michael makes his big announcement that he wants a vote
她说在8分39秒，当迈克尔宣布他要投票

812
00:38:29.540 --> 00:38:35.460
on who is the true Santa, Mindy said, and I'm quoting her, one of the great legacies of
选出谁才是真正的圣诞老人时，敏迪说——我引用她的话——这部剧最伟大的遗产之一

813
00:38:35.460 --> 00:38:38.800
the show is the announcements outside of Michael's office.
就是迈克尔办公室外的那些公告。

814
00:38:38.800 --> 00:38:42.920
She goes on to say, I used to call it Act Break Alley.
她接着说，我以前管那儿叫“幕间休息巷”。

815
00:38:43.100 --> 00:38:47.600
The writers would have Michael come out of his office, make an announcement, and that would
编剧们会让迈克尔走出办公室，发布一个公告，而那

816
00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:48.960
often lead to the act break.
通常会引出幕间休息。

817
00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:51.140
And that's exactly what happens here.
这儿发生的情况正是如此。

818
00:38:51.260 --> 00:38:51.720
It's true.
确实如此。

819
00:38:52.260 --> 00:38:54.780
So you got a little act break alley there.
所以你在这儿看到了一个小小的“幕间休息巷”。

820
00:38:56.040 --> 00:39:00.480
Dwight is convinced that his secret Santa is sending him pieces of a gun.
德怀特坚信他的秘密圣诞老人正在给他寄一把枪的零件。

821
00:39:00.860 --> 00:39:03.320
But this last piece doesn't make any sense.
但这最后一件零件完全说不通。

822
00:39:03.520 --> 00:39:05.040
Why did they send him a dial?
他们为什么要寄给他一个拨盘？

823
00:39:05.220 --> 00:39:06.420
They should have sent him a trigger.
他们应该寄给他一个扳机才对。

824
00:39:07.100 --> 00:39:09.940
And Meredith and Phyllis are like, why do you think it's a gun?
梅雷迪斯和菲利斯就问，你为什么觉得那是把枪？

825
00:39:10.600 --> 00:39:16.120
And then Stanley has a great line where he says, unless the missing piece is a gun, you
然后斯坦利有一句很棒的台词，他说，除非缺的那块是枪，否则

826
00:39:16.120 --> 00:39:17.100
don't have a gun.
你根本就没有枪。

827
00:39:18.040 --> 00:39:20.180
I don't know why that tickles me so much.
我不知道为什么这句话让我觉得这么好笑。

828
00:39:20.560 --> 00:39:21.880
His delivery was so good.
他的演绎太到位了。

829
00:39:22.300 --> 00:39:24.680
We got a fan question from Beth G.
我们收到了一位粉丝贝丝·G的提问，

830
00:39:24.880 --> 00:39:25.920
in Olympia, Washington.
她来自华盛顿州的奥林匹亚。

831
00:39:26.180 --> 00:39:33.540
Who came up with the list of Dwight's speculations on what his Christmas present might be as he builds
是谁想出了德怀特在拼装礼物时，对他圣诞礼物可能是什么的那些猜测清单？

832
00:39:33.540 --> 00:39:33.800
it?
你知道，他手里有张写着清单的纸。

833
00:39:34.140 --> 00:39:36.580
You know, he has that piece of paper with the liSt.
你知道，他手里有张写着清单的纸。

834
00:39:36.660 --> 00:39:40.200
And Beth said, I never noticed that speculum was on the liSt.
贝丝说，我以前从没注意到清单上有“窥镜”这个词。

835
00:39:40.380 --> 00:39:44.420
But during a recent rewatch, I noticed and almost died laughing.
但最近重看的时候，我注意到了，差点笑死。

836
00:39:44.880 --> 00:39:49.060
So I found a list of all the things that Dwight thinks.
所以我找到了德怀特想到的所有东西的清单。

837
00:39:49.220 --> 00:39:50.700
This is what's on his piece of paper.
这就是他那张纸上写的内容。

838
00:39:50.900 --> 00:39:51.260
Okay.
好的。

839
00:39:51.520 --> 00:39:53.820
In answer to your question, Beth, this would be the writers.
回答你的问题，贝丝，这应该是编剧们想出来的。

840
00:39:54.100 --> 00:39:55.640
The writers would have come up with this liSt.
清单应该是编剧们写的。

841
00:39:55.640 --> 00:39:59.900
Phil Shea would have gone to the writers and said, what do you want me to write on this
菲尔·谢伊会去问编剧们，你们想让我在这张

842
00:39:59.900 --> 00:40:01.140
piece of paper for Dwight?
纸上给德怀特写点什么？

843
00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:05.800
And he would have had to write this list over and over and over and over again on various
然后他得在各种纸垫上一遍又一遍地写下这个清单，

844
00:40:05.800 --> 00:40:09.740
pads of paper because every take, Rain was going to scratch one out.
因为每一条拍摄，雷恩都要划掉一项。

845
00:40:09.900 --> 00:40:13.440
So here was the list of things that Dwight thought this might be.
所以这就是德怀特认为这东西可能是的清单。

846
00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:22.940
An aardvark trap, beaver trap, gun, chipmunk trap, possum trap, skunk trap, lobster trap,
土豚陷阱、海狸陷阱、枪、花栗鼠陷阱、负鼠陷阱、臭鼬陷阱、龙虾陷阱、

847
00:40:22.940 --> 00:40:28.140
man trap, lathe, abdominizer, speculum.
捕人陷阱、车床、腹肌训练器、窥镜。

848
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:33.820
He was mostly convinced it was some sort of trap, an animal trap.
他基本认定这是某种陷阱，一种动物陷阱。

849
00:40:35.780 --> 00:40:39.720
Santa Phyllis is now going to do the tree lighting reveal.
圣诞老人菲利斯现在要进行点灯仪式了。

850
00:40:39.980 --> 00:40:41.960
And it's so festive and cheery.
看起来真是又喜庆又欢快。

851
00:40:42.080 --> 00:40:43.380
I love Phyllis in this scene.
我超爱这一幕里的菲利斯。

852
00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:44.000
I know.
我知道。

853
00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:45.280
I absolutely love it.
我真的太爱这一幕了。

854
00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:47.840
Michael is starting to get real sour.
迈克尔开始变得很不爽了。

855
00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:49.080
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

856
00:40:49.560 --> 00:40:52.100
So he has this talking head.
所以他有段对着镜头的独白。

857
00:40:52.940 --> 00:40:57.920
Where he says, I don't need a lot for Christmas, like diamonds or brooch, pendants.
他说，我圣诞节不需要什么贵重礼物，比如钻石、胸针或吊坠。

858
00:40:58.400 --> 00:41:00.400
He just wants to be Santa.
他只想当圣诞老人。

859
00:41:00.900 --> 00:41:06.380
And this whole time, he is, like, reversing his Santa costume.
而在这期间，他一直在把他的圣诞老人装反着穿。

860
00:41:06.620 --> 00:41:11.580
Taking this decorative Christmas robe off his credenza, making it into a belt.
从办公桌柜上拿过那件装饰用的圣诞长袍，把它当成腰带系上。

861
00:41:11.800 --> 00:41:14.780
I want to give a shout out to Steve's skills right here.
我得特别夸一下史蒂夫在这里展现的功力。

862
00:41:14.920 --> 00:41:16.480
I put it in my document.
我把它记在我的文档里了。

863
00:41:16.480 --> 00:41:20.040
I need everyone to appreciate how hard this is to do.
我需要每个人都意识到这有多难做到。

864
00:41:20.040 --> 00:41:21.440
Yes, I wrote it, too.
没错，我也写下来了。

865
00:41:21.560 --> 00:41:23.240
I put two little stars by it.
我在旁边标了两颗小星星。

866
00:41:23.320 --> 00:41:25.480
I said, go to 9 minutes, 52 seconds.
我说，去看9分52秒处。

867
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:27.920
Michael goes from Santa to Jesus.
迈克尔从圣诞老人变成了耶稣。

868
00:41:28.140 --> 00:41:34.100
And Steve had to do all the dialogue, change his outfit, put the belt on in one shot.
史蒂夫必须在这一镜到底中完成所有台词、更换服装并系好腰带。

869
00:41:34.220 --> 00:41:35.320
There are no cutaways.
中间没有任何剪辑。

870
00:41:36.140 --> 00:41:37.440
This is truly amazing.
这真的太厉害了。

871
00:41:37.440 --> 00:41:43.800
I cannot express to you how hard it is to do even ordinary business while you're acting.
我无法向你们表达，在演戏的同时还要处理日常琐事有多难。

872
00:41:44.080 --> 00:41:50.040
How many times would I have to do a scene where I'm supposed to walk in with a bag of groceries,
我得拍多少次那种戏，就是我得提着一袋杂货走进来，

873
00:41:50.340 --> 00:41:52.720
set it down, and take some items out of the bag?
放下袋子，再从里面拿出几样东西？

874
00:41:53.140 --> 00:41:55.880
Suddenly, I am incapable of doing that action.
突然之间，我就完全不会做那个动作了。

875
00:41:55.880 --> 00:42:01.220
I multitask in my kitchen constantly, and I'm always thinking about it, too.
我在厨房里经常一心多用，而且我总是会去想这件事。

876
00:42:01.400 --> 00:42:06.720
Like, as I'm, like, shutting the fridge with my foot while scrambling an egg and drinking coffee
比如，当我一边用脚关冰箱，一边炒鸡蛋，一边喝咖啡，

877
00:42:06.720 --> 00:42:11.740
and, like, organizing some homework papers in the morning and holding a conversation,
还要在早上整理作业纸，同时进行对话时，

878
00:42:11.740 --> 00:42:15.780
I think to myself, if this was written out for me, I could never do it.
我心想，如果这些动作被写进剧本里，我绝对做不到。

879
00:42:15.900 --> 00:42:16.820
I don't know what it is.
我也不知道为什么。

880
00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:19.900
It's so hard just to memorize your lines and say them truthfully.
光是记住台词并真诚地讲出来就已经很难了。

881
00:42:20.660 --> 00:42:24.240
This amount of business is—people should study it.
这种动作戏——人们真该好好研究一下。

882
00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:25.200
He does such a good job.
他做得太棒了。

883
00:42:25.880 --> 00:42:27.020
And with comic timing.
而且还把握住了喜剧节奏。

884
00:42:27.260 --> 00:42:27.780
I know.
我知道。

885
00:42:27.880 --> 00:42:31.980
I always think of this when I would watch shows like ER or Grey's Anatomy,
我每次看《急诊室的故事》或《实习医生格蕾》这类剧时都会想到这一点，

886
00:42:32.140 --> 00:42:34.660
when they have the gurney flying through the hallway,
当他们推着担架车在走廊里飞奔时，

887
00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:37.840
and they're yelling out all of this medical jargon, like,
他们在大声喊着各种医学术语，比如，

888
00:42:38.060 --> 00:42:41.360
stick to me this, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, and they're, like, having to do all this action.
给我这个，巴拉巴拉之类的，他们还得同时做那么多动作。

889
00:42:41.360 --> 00:42:43.880
I'm like, well, that'll be a job I never have because—
我就想，好吧，那是我永远干不了的工作，因为——

890
00:42:43.880 --> 00:42:44.100
Yes.
没错。

891
00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:46.560
That's a lot of talking and moving at the same time.
又要说话又要走位，这太难了。

